//
// Conduit Path B (--use-conduit, fix landed at e2ea0ab450) end-to-end
// xfail for the per-launch release BD-pool pattern.  npu2 only (Path B
// sprint context: npu2 is the LM-head target).
//
// --dma-task-to-conduit ERASES the IRON-emitted inline await/free ops
// (ConduitDmaTaskToConduit.cpp:48,403-415).  --conduit-to-dma re-emits
// all releases at end-of-rtSeq (Step 8g, "Path B").  At this shape
// (4 launches × 5 same-channel MM2S = 20 same-channel configures, no
// inline release between them) the per-channel BD live-interval set
// fully overlaps and exceeds the 16-BD per-channel shim pool on npu2.
//
// Expected today: aiecc.py exits non-zero with the verbatim allocator
// diagnostic from
// lib/Dialect/AIEX/Transforms/AIEAssignRuntimeSequenceBDIDs.cpp:106-113
// (`emitOpError` is on the runtime_sequence's containing op which lives
// on shim tile (0, 0); MM2S input channel index is 0).
//
// AFTER PATH C LANDS (basic Path C is in flight at Task #18; full Path
// C will preserve IRON's release boundaries via
// conduit.wait_all{token = bool}), this lit MUST be flipped: replace
// the `not aiecc + FileCheck` block below with the same `clang
// %S/test.cpp ... ; %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE
// -i insts.bin` block from stateful.lit.  After Path C the test
// verifies conduit produces byte-equivalent output to stateful at this
// shape.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% not %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir 2>&1 | FileCheck %s

// CHECK: Allocator exhausted available buffer descriptor IDs for channel 0 on tile (0, 0)
// CHECK: Live BD intervals exceed the per-channel pool capacity
